+## Retry or fail fast
+
+Work through this every time a call fails, before you send it again.
+
+```dot
+digraph retry_or_fail_fast {
+    "HTTP call failed or timed out" [shape=ellipse];
+    "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health" [shape=plaintext];
+    "Did the health check exit 0?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Is the request a POST?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Does the POST have an Idempotency-Key header?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Never retry a POST without an idempotency key" [shape=octagon, style=filled, fillcolor=red, fontcolor=white];
+    "Is the response 502, 503, 504 or a timeout?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Does the response have a Retry-After header?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Wait the Retry-After time" [shape=box];
+    "Retry up to 3 times after 1 s, 2 s and 4 s, same key" [shape=box];
+    "Fail fast and report the error" [shape=doublecircle];
+    "Request retried" [shape=doublecircle];
+
+    "HTTP call failed or timed out" -> "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health";
+    "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health" -> "Did the health check exit 0?";
+    "Did the health check exit 0?" -> "Fail fast and report the error" [label="no: service is down"];
+    "Did the health check exit 0?" -> "Is the request a POST?" [label="yes"];
+    "Is the request a POST?" -> "Does the POST have an Idempotency-Key header?" [label="yes"];
+    "Is the request a POST?" -> "Is the response 502, 503, 504 or a timeout?" [label="no: GET, HEAD, PUT, DELETE"];
+    "Does the POST have an Idempotency-Key header?" -> "Never retry a POST without an idempotency key" [label="no"];
+    "Never retry a POST without an idempotency key" -> "Fail fast and report the error";
+    "Does the POST have an Idempotency-Key header?" -> "Is the response 502, 503, 504 or a timeout?" [label="yes"];
+    "Is the response 502, 503, 504 or a timeout?" -> "Fail fast and report the error" [label="no: 4xx, fix the request"];
+    "Is the response 502, 503, 504 or a timeout?" -> "Does the response have a Retry-After header?" [label="yes"];
+    "Does the response have a Retry-After header?" -> "Wait the Retry-After time" [label="yes"];
+    "Does the response have a Retry-After header?" -> "Retry up to 3 times after 1 s, 2 s and 4 s, same key" [label="no"];
+    "Wait the Retry-After time" -> "Retry up to 3 times after 1 s, 2 s and 4 s, same key";
+    "Retry up to 3 times after 1 s, 2 s and 4 s, same key" -> "Request retried";
+}
+```
+
+The key check comes before the status check. A POST with no key fails fast even on a 503 or a timeout.
+
